title: 'sc-hop: add Prometheus metrics'
doc:
  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      Adds Prometheus metrics to sc-hop:

      - `substrate_hop_pool_bytes` / `substrate_hop_pool_max_bytes` — gauges.
      - `substrate_hop_pool_inserted_bytes_total` — counter.
      - `substrate_hop_pool_removed_total` — counter, label `reason` one of: `acked`, `expired_promoted`, `expired_unpromoted`, `corrupt`, `startup_dropped`. All series are pre-created at registration so the first data-loss event is visible to `rate()`. `expired_unpromoted` is an upper bound on loss: re-checking stops at `MAX_PROMOTION_ATTEMPTS`, so a final submission that landed on-chain still counts.
      - `substrate_hop_rpc_errors_total` — counter, labels `method` (wire names, joining the RPC middleware's `substrate_rpc_calls_*`) and `reason` (`HopError` variant).
      - `substrate_hop_promotions_confirmed_total` — counter.
      - `substrate_hop_promotion_backlog` — gauge, snapshot once per maintenance cycle; includes entries that are backing off.
      - `substrate_hop_maintenance_ticks_total` — counter (maintenance-loop liveness).

      `HopParams::build_pool` gains an `Option<&Registry>` parameter, `HopDataPool::new` a `HopMetrics` one, and `HopDataPool::cleanup_expired` a promotion-window one that scopes only the backlog gauge; a registration failure only disables metrics. The omni-node passes its existing registry. See the crate README's Metrics section.
crates:
  - name: sc-hop
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
    bump: patch
